# MQTT Reliability Patterns

## Connection Management
- Implement automatic reconnection with exponential backoff
- Handle `Incoming::Disconnect` events gracefully
- Use configurable reconnection delays from [src/config.rs](mdc:src/config.rs)

## Circuit Breaker Implementation
- Use the `CircuitBreaker` struct to prevent cascading failures
- Monitor failure counts and implement state transitions
- Reject requests when circuit is open to protect system resources

## Error Recovery
- Implement retry logic with configurable `max_retries`
- Track consecutive failures and trigger circuit breaker when threshold is exceeded
- Use exponential backoff for retry attempts

## Message Publishing
- Handle publish failures gracefully without terminating the sender loop
- Log errors and continue processing other messages
- Implement proper QoS handling for message delivery guarantees

## Health Monitoring
- Expose circuit breaker status through `get_circuit_breaker_info()`
- Monitor channel health to prevent buffer overflows
- Log health status for debugging and monitoring
